id: pm-oahhyc
title: "Dynamic-read continuation cursors are born stale: pm health emits a cursor that its next invocation rejects"
description: "A default-budget full pm health read returns a valid-looking output continuation for the remaining checks, but an immediate retry with that cursor fails read_output_cursor_stale even though no tracker mutation occurred. Dynamic health fields such as telemetry timestamps make the collection fingerprint change between pages, so the token-efficient recovery path is unusable and the only successful workaround is an unbounded reread."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[9]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",context-management,cursor,diagnostics,output-contract,regression,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-08-24T14:24:39.321Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-24T14:24:39.321Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: Dynamic read pagination binds every page to a stable snapshot or epoch whose identity survives volatile telemetry and clock fields; The exact emitted CLI recovery command succeeds without a tracker mutation and SDK and MCP cursor bindings behave identically; A deterministic regression advances health telemetry and clock fields between page one and page two while preserving the declared row collection; Cursor fingerprints include only collection identity and immutable query inputs or the producer freezes volatile inputs for the continuation lifetime; Stale cursors from genuine tracker or contract changes still fail closed with an executable restart command; Default-budget and unbounded reads are set-equivalent and do not duplicate or skip checks
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make every declared bounded-read continuation executable and snapshot-consistent across dynamic diagnostic surfaces
value: Agents can recover omitted health and diagnostic rows without discarding the first page or paying for an unbounded rerun
why_now: The complete ecosystem review exercised the recovery command exactly as emitted and it failed immediately on the current release
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
expected_result: An output cursor returned by pm health resumes the exact declared check collection on the next invocation and returns the remaining rows with stable snapshot semantics.
actual_result: pm health --check-only --full returned five of ten checks and a recovery cursor; the immediate retry returned read_output_cursor_stale. Re-running with --output-budget unbounded returned all ten checks successfully.
affected_version: 2026.8.24
component: read-output continuation
regression: true
